+# Privacy audit and maintenance
+
+Reviewed: 2026-11-11. Scope: all checked-in website HTML, CSS, assets, scripts,
+package configuration, and hosting headers. This is a source audit and static
+regression check; no browser, live traffic, or hosting dashboard was inspected.
+
+## Data and third-party inventory
+
+| Item | Finding and mitigation |
+| --- | --- |
+| Hero photograph | Previously loaded from `images.unsplash.com`, exposing each visitor's IP, browser request headers, and potentially referrer information to a third party. The same stock image is now stored in `assets/coffee-hero.jpg` and delivered from this origin. Original source: https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1495474472287-4d71bcdd2085?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1350&q=80 |
+| Fonts and styling | System fonts and a local stylesheet; no font CDN. Inline styles moved into CSS so CSP can block injected inline styling. |
+| Client-side scripts | None existed and none are needed. CSP denies scripts, inline handlers, workers, network APIs, forms, frames, and plugins. No cookies, Web Storage, IndexedDB, service workers, identifiers, fingerprinting, beacons, or analytics are created by this site. |
+| Third-party embeds and links | No embeds, trackers, remote subresources, resource hints, or outbound links in website pages. CSP violation reporting is deliberately omitted: there is no collector, and adding one would create a new data flow. |
+| Dependencies | No production or build dependencies. The existing `start` command downloads `statikk` through `pnpm dlx` as a local serving tool; it is not shipped to visitors and was not executed in this audit. Production builds use only Node built-ins. |
+| Hosting | Requests necessarily disclose IP addresses, paths, and ordinary request headers to the hosting infrastructure. Provider-side logging, retention, TLS setup, cookies injected by a CDN, and analytics injection are outside this repository and remain deployment responsibilities. |
+| Navigation | Existing account, rewards, logout, ordering, and contact links are placeholders with no backing services in this repository. No session handling, personal-data collection, or account rights workflow is claimed. The privacy link now resolves to a real static page. |
+
+## Enforced defaults
+
+- `_headers` applies CSP, no-referrer, permissions restrictions, MIME protection,
+  framing protection, opener/resource isolation, and DNS-prefetch suppression to
+  all paths on compatible static hosts. HTML includes an early CSP and referrer
+  fallback; framing, permissions, HSTS, and other HTTP-only policies need real
+  response headers. CSP is enforced immediately because the entire site has been
+  inventoried and has no executable dependencies.
+- HSTS starts at 300 seconds without `includeSubDomains` or preload because the
+  production domain and its subdomains are unknown. Serve over HTTPS, redirect
+  HTTP at the host, and increase the lifetime after validating TLS deployment.
+- Sensitive data is minimized by collecting and storing none in this static
+  implementation. No consent cookie or consent-management SDK is necessary.
+- The build publishes an explicit file allowlist, excluding `.git`, package
+  metadata, tests, internal documentation, and build scripts.
+
+## Review gate for future changes
+
+Run `npm test` and `npm run build` for each change. Re-audit this inventory before
+introducing any dependency, script, form, external link, image host, analytics,
+payment integration, or embed. The static tests intentionally reject those
+changes until their data flows and required CSP exceptions have been reviewed.
+They are regression checks for this small site, not a general HTML security parser.
+
+If collection is introduced, document each field's immediate purpose and deletion
+deadline, collect only required fields, and explain that purpose at the input.
+Offer guest use where possible. Do not place personal information or tokens in
+URLs, browser storage, analytics, application logs, or CSP reports. Validate and
+authorize on the server; encode text safely instead of using HTML string sinks.
+Use HTTPS and server-managed `Secure; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax; Path=/` session
+cookies (prefer `__Host-` names without `Domain`). Do not implement authentication
+with browser storage. Real logout must revoke the server session, expire cookies,
+send `Cache-Control: no-store`, and return an appropriately scoped
+`Clear-Site-Data: "cookies", "storage", "cache"` response. Do not clear data on
+ordinary public page loads or treat a static logout link as session termination.
+
+Review hosting logs before launch: disable optional analytics, avoid recording
+query strings, cookies, authorization headers, or request bodies, restrict access,
+and configure the shortest operational retention. Document actual retention and
+a working data-rights contact in the public notice when a provider and operator
+are selected. Review providers and their logging/retention settings regularly and
+after configuration changes. Do not promise provider-level retention guarantees
+that have not been verified.
