+# The Daily Grind
+
+A static coffee-shop website with privacy-protective defaults. Node.js 20+ is
+required for tooling; there are no build dependencies to install.
+
+```sh
+npm test
+npm run build
+```
+
+Publish only `dist/`. `netlify.toml` configures the build and publish directory
+for Netlify; Cloudflare Pages can use the same commands and directory. Both
+consume the generated `dist/_headers`. On any other host, translate `_headers`
+into its response-header configuration; copying that file alone will not set
+headers unless the host supports it. Serve over HTTPS with HTTP-to-HTTPS
+redirection at the edge. Do not enable automatic analytics or script injection.
+
+HTML includes CSP and referrer-policy fallbacks. HTTP headers are still required
+for complete protection, particularly framing, permissions, MIME handling, and
+HSTS. The existing `start` command is a local convenience and is not a production
+security-header configuration. Do not publish the repository root.
+
+The homepage design and navigation are retained. Only `/` and `/privacy-policy/`
+are implemented here; other pre-existing navigation destinations require separate
+services. See [the privacy audit](PRIVACY-AUDIT.md) for the resource inventory,
+hosting responsibilities, and secure data-handling requirements for future work.
+
+Header behavior reference: [MDN CSP guide](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Guides/CSP).
+In particular, `frame-ancestors` must be delivered as an HTTP header, not a meta tag.
